WEBVTT

1
00:58:34.082 --> 00:58:35.082
Hallelujah.

2
00:58:35.082 --> 00:58:39.922
Hey, I want to specifically speak this prayer over the church.

3
00:58:39.922 --> 00:58:47.122
If you are such a person, whose speaking still needs to change, you don't need to raise your hand.

4
00:58:47.122 --> 00:58:48.122
This is not about embarrassment, this is not about condemnation.

5
00:58:48.122 --> 00:58:51.882
But if your tongue still needs to change to the kingdom of God, then agree with me in this prayer.

6
00:58:51.882 --> 00:58:58.082
You know, I also had to make a choice not to curse anymore.

7
00:58:58.082 --> 00:58:59.482
I had to make a choice not to speak stupid jokes anymore.

8
00:58:59.482 --> 00:59:05.202
I just brought this into my life.

9
00:59:05.202 --> 00:59:08.762
Those were traditions in my life.

10
00:59:08.762 --> 00:59:12.242
I had to come to repentance from that.

11
00:59:12.242 --> 00:59:14.162
And you know, you don't have to be ashamed of it, we just need to change it.

12
00:59:14.162 --> 00:59:16.242
So if there are things in your speech that still need to change, an occasional curse word,

13
00:59:16.242 --> 00:59:20.122
an occasional swear word, an occasional lie, an occasional gossip, an occasional statement

14
00:59:20.122 --> 00:59:27.122
that is totally inappropriate.

15
00:59:27.122 --> 00:59:33.522
If you are such a person, just close your eyes for a moment.

16
00:59:33.522 --> 00:59:35.242
Lord, I want to pray that today is a day of repentance, that today in the name of Jesus

17
00:59:35.242 --> 00:59:38.602
at this moment tongues will be cleansed in Jesus' name.

18
00:59:38.602 --> 00:59:49.162
And I see Jesus going around healing people at this moment and freeing people from talk.

19
00:59:49.162 --> 00:59:56.202


20
00:59:56.202 --> 01:00:04.442


21
01:00:04.442 --> 01:00:06.882
that we should not speak in God's kingdom.

22
01:00:06.882 --> 01:00:13.802
Words of unforgiveness, stop now in the name of Jesus.

23
01:00:13.802 --> 01:00:18.762
Words of fear, stop today in the name of Jesus.

24
01:00:19.362 --> 01:00:24.562
Words of unbelief, stop today in the name of Jesus.

25
01:00:24.562 --> 01:00:29.602
Cursing must stop now in the name of Jesus.

26
01:00:29.602 --> 01:00:38.162
Jokes that seem funny, but do not fit in the presence of our King and Lord,

27
01:00:38.162 --> 01:00:40.562
it stops today in the name of Jesus.

28
01:00:40.562 --> 01:00:47.322
And I want to motivate our hearts in Jesus' name that we make that choice today to

29
01:00:47.322 --> 01:00:48.322
draw a line.

30
01:00:48.322 --> 01:00:52.082
This was it and now it stops.

31
01:00:52.082 --> 01:00:57.402
From today my humor is compatible with Jesus.

32
01:00:57.402 --> 01:01:04.562
From today my way of speaking is compatible with the presence of King Jesus.

33
01:01:04.562 --> 01:01:10.562
What I say from today, Jesus is always with us.

34
01:01:10.562 --> 01:01:13.202
But I will indulge in a fantasy now.

35
01:01:13.202 --> 01:01:18.922
Imagine if He were to change into a physical form, you would see Him standing now.

36
01:01:18.922 --> 01:01:24.642
What would you still say and what would you no longer say in His presence?

37
01:01:24.642 --> 01:01:31.002
And I declare in Jesus' name that that authority will rest upon you from now on.

38
01:01:31.002 --> 01:01:32.602
For it is possible.

39
01:01:32.602 --> 01:01:34.762
He is unbound.

40
01:01:34.762 --> 01:01:37.482
I call upon King Jesus.

41
01:01:37.482 --> 01:01:39.962
Not on us.

42
01:01:39.962 --> 01:01:41.962
We are not unredeemed.

43
01:01:42.282 --> 01:01:43.282
He is it.

44
01:01:43.282 --> 01:01:44.482
He can change it in your life.

45
01:01:44.482 --> 01:01:49.922
Can I get an amen from the people who meant this prayer for themselves?

46
01:01:49.922 --> 01:01:51.482
In the name of Jesus.

47
01:01:51.482 --> 01:01:52.482
Amen?

48
01:01:52.482 --> 01:01:53.482
Amen.

49
01:01:53.482 --> 01:01:54.482
In Jesus' name.

50
01:01:54.482 --> 01:01:55.482
Hallelujah.

51
01:01:55.482 --> 01:01:57.482
Shall we give King Jesus a thunderous applause?

52
01:01:57.482 --> 01:01:58.482
Hallelujah.

53
01:01:58.482 --> 01:01:59.482
Fight dust.

54
01:01:59.482 --> 01:02:00.482
Hallelujah.

55
01:02:08.482 --> 01:02:09.482
Dust poop.

56
01:02:12.482 --> 01:02:13.482
Hallelujah.

57
01:02:15.482 --> 01:02:18.282
That went well today with those parking spaces.

58
01:02:18.282 --> 01:02:20.682
Are you starting about that again?

59
01:02:20.682 --> 01:02:22.482
Yes, I am excited about that.

60
01:02:22.482 --> 01:02:24.202
I am super excited about that.

61
01:02:24.202 --> 01:02:29.482
The people who helped out this week, for example Jan.

62
01:02:29.482 --> 01:02:31.482
And Jan said, oh don't mention me.

63
01:02:31.482 --> 01:02:32.482
Jan, Jan, Jan.

64
01:02:32.482 --> 01:02:34.482
Jan, Jan, Jan, Jan, Jan.

65
01:02:35.002 --> 01:02:45.002
Jan, I'll call him this week and I'll say, can you with the digger, can you prepare those parking spaces?

66
01:02:45.002 --> 01:02:46.002
Can you get them ready?

67
01:02:46.002 --> 01:02:51.562
Because that construction road was laid out, but next to it you often have the ground being very uneven, very muddy, so that wasn't a good place to park your car yet.

68
01:02:51.562 --> 01:02:58.002
So I asked Jan, can you help out?

69
01:02:58.002 --> 01:03:01.002
Yes, I can.

70
01:03:01.002 --> 01:03:02.002
I said, when can that be?

71
01:03:02.002 --> 01:03:04.002
Now?

72
01:03:04.002 --> 01:03:05.002
Okay, great.

73
01:03:05.002 --> 01:03:06.002
And I think it's so cool that people make themselves available.

74
01:03:06.002 --> 01:03:10.002
Here’s one, Frans.

75
01:03:10.002 --> 01:03:12.002
That man puts in more hours than anyone else combined at Open Church.

76
01:03:12.002 --> 01:03:16.002
Can I get a round of applause for this guy?

77
01:03:16.002 --> 01:03:18.002
It's really amazing.

78
01:03:22.002 --> 01:03:24.002
Edda and, Edda.

79
01:03:24.002 --> 01:03:26.002
Eddie and Lisa.

80
01:03:26.002 --> 01:03:28.002


81
01:03:28.002 --> 01:03:30.002
Is Edda in the name of Jesus.

82
01:03:31.002 --> 01:03:32.002
That's just right.

83
01:03:32.002 --> 01:03:33.002
There's nothing wrong with it.

84
01:03:33.002 --> 01:03:39.002
Eddie and Lisa, they are helping with parking today, for which many thanks.

85
01:03:39.002 --> 01:03:44.002
But this is really just to indicate how we will do it in the coming time.

86
01:03:44.002 --> 01:03:46.002
Because here is already a preview.

87
01:03:46.002 --> 01:03:51.002
When we eventually lay out the real parking spaces, this is what it will look like.

88
01:03:51.002 --> 01:03:53.002
This is how it will be.

89
01:03:53.002 --> 01:03:55.002
Only it will get even better.

90
01:03:55.002 --> 01:04:01.002
Next week we will lay gravel and rubble, so that the cars do not have to stand in the black sand.

91
01:04:01.002 --> 01:04:03.002
Then you will be on rubble.

92
01:04:03.002 --> 01:04:04.002
That is better for all of us and for the cleaning team in the church.

93
01:04:04.002 --> 01:04:09.002
But I just think it's super cool how we are building everything step by step.

94
01:04:09.002 --> 01:04:15.002
And that involves all of us in a process.

95
01:04:15.002 --> 01:04:18.002
And I think it's super cool.

96
01:04:18.002 --> 01:04:20.002
So applause once again for everyone who is helping, please.

97
01:04:20.002 --> 01:04:23.002
This is really super cool.

98
01:04:23.002 --> 01:04:24.002
Good morning.

99
01:04:29.002 --> 01:04:30.002
Delightful.

100
01:04:31.002 --> 01:04:32.002


101
01:04:32.002 --> 01:04:33.002
What a worship.

102
01:04:33.002 --> 01:04:35.002
God is so good.

103
01:04:35.002 --> 01:04:39.002
I have the honor of announcing the collection this morning.

104
01:04:39.002 --> 01:04:40.002
Hallelujah, Frans.

105
01:04:40.002 --> 01:04:42.002
I completely agree with you.

106
01:04:42.002 --> 01:04:50.002
And the beautiful thing is, we always have the worship in the middle, actually the collection in the middle

107
01:04:50.002 --> 01:04:51.002
of the worship.

108
01:04:51.002 --> 01:04:54.002
And actually that is also what God wants.

109
01:04:54.002 --> 01:04:56.002
Because it just belongs together.

110
01:04:56.002 --> 01:04:58.002
It is actually just worship.

111
01:04:59.002 --> 01:05:05.002
And the beautiful thing is, the text I have for today, I was looking into.

112
01:05:05.002 --> 01:05:08.002
And I first took it from the basic Bible.

113
01:05:08.002 --> 01:05:11.002
And then I was working on it a bit more.

114
01:05:11.002 --> 01:05:15.002
I think, after all, basic Bible, maybe also the NBV.

115
01:05:15.002 --> 01:05:18.002
I don't know if the text could be projected.

116
01:05:18.002 --> 01:05:19.002
Great.

117
01:05:19.002 --> 01:05:21.002
Oh yes, here it is.

118
01:05:23.002 --> 01:05:24.002
Let me see.

119
01:05:24.002 --> 01:05:25.002
Yes, this is the basic Bible.

120
01:05:25.002 --> 01:05:26.002
This is the basic Bible.

121
01:05:26.002 --> 01:05:30.002
He says, give, and then it will be given to you, a good measure, pressed down,

122
01:05:30.002 --> 01:05:33.002
shaken together, running over will be given to you by people.

123
01:05:33.002 --> 01:05:37.002
For with the measure you use, it will be measured to you.

124
01:05:37.002 --> 01:05:39.002
Actually, that is not true.

125
01:05:41.002 --> 01:05:42.002
No, no.

126
01:05:42.002 --> 01:05:45.002
For just put the NBV on, if you want.

127
01:05:46.002 --> 01:05:50.002
It says give, and it will be given to you, a good, firmly pressed, well-shaken

128
01:05:50.002 --> 01:05:53.002
and overflowing measure will be assigned to you.

129
01:05:53.002 --> 01:05:57.002
For the measure you use for others will also be used for you.

130
01:05:58.002 --> 01:05:59.002
Do you see what is missing?

131
01:06:00.002 --> 01:06:01.002
The word people.

132
01:06:03.002 --> 01:06:10.002
For here in the basic Bible it says overflowing measures will be given to you by people.

133
01:06:11.002 --> 01:06:12.002
That is simply not true.

134
01:06:12.002 --> 01:06:13.002
That is not always true.

135
01:06:14.002 --> 01:06:15.002
Far from always true.

136
01:06:17.002 --> 01:06:20.002
And the point is, yes, I don't want to pat myself on the shoulder.

137
01:06:21.002 --> 01:06:22.002
No, that's not what it's about.

138
01:06:22.002 --> 01:06:24.002
But you do need to pay attention when reading the Bible.

139
01:06:25.002 --> 01:06:29.002
For the people who translate the Bible are truly precious people.

140
01:06:29.002 --> 01:06:30.002
But we are all human.

141
01:06:31.002 --> 01:06:33.002
And therefore it is good to lay other translations side by side.

142
01:06:34.002 --> 01:06:42.002
For know that if you just go, and if you just go give, the Father will take care of you.

143
01:06:43.002 --> 01:06:45.002
So I wanted to set that straight for a moment.

144
01:06:45.002 --> 01:06:49.002
Not only for myself, but actually for all of us.

145
01:06:50.002 --> 01:06:53.002
We should not expect anything back from people when we give or bring back.

146
01:06:54.002 --> 01:06:55.002
We must expect from God.

147
01:06:57.002 --> 01:07:06.002
And this passage, Luke 6, starting from verse 20 and so on, is actually Matthew 5 in short,

148
01:07:07.002 --> 01:07:10.002
which Pastor Vanessa has often spoken about.

149
01:07:11.002 --> 01:07:12.002
And what is that actually about?

150
01:07:12.002 --> 01:07:13.002
And what is that actually about?

151
01:07:13.002 --> 01:07:15.002
It is about the kingdom of God within us.

152
01:07:17.002 --> 01:07:18.002
And that is the big picture.

153
01:07:18.002 --> 01:07:19.002
You cannot do that halfway.

154
01:07:21.002 --> 01:07:23.002
And that is also the case with giving or bringing back.

155
01:07:24.002 --> 01:07:29.002
For when we give or bring back, when we sow time in our relationship with the Father,

156
01:07:29.002 --> 01:07:30.002
with prayer, worship, and the Word.

157
01:07:31.002 --> 01:07:34.002
And then also with each other, that is also horizontal.

158
01:07:34.002 --> 01:07:38.002
Distributing love, sowing love and prayer among the people around us for each other.

159
01:07:38.002 --> 01:07:40.002
For friend and foe.

160
01:07:41.002 --> 01:07:44.002
Sowing work in this world in the name of Jesus.

161
01:07:44.002 --> 01:07:45.002
Building together, everything.

162
01:07:46.002 --> 01:07:47.002
Sowing resources in God's kingdom.

163
01:07:48.002 --> 01:07:52.002
That is what Matthew 5 breathes out.

164
01:07:53.002 --> 01:07:56.002
And that does not happen from us; there is nothing of humans involved.

165
01:07:57.002 --> 01:08:01.002
I want to make this very clear this morning, because there is also nothing of us in it.

166
01:08:02.002 --> 01:08:08.002
Everything we are, what we have, every breath we breathe out, comes from Him.

167
01:08:10.002 --> 01:08:11.002
That is very basic.

168
01:08:12.002 --> 01:08:15.002
Every millisecond that we live also comes from Him.

169
01:08:15.002 --> 01:08:17.002
Our whole life is already His.

170
01:08:18.002 --> 01:08:22.002
And He has redeemed us, He has paid for us and restored us in honor.

171
01:08:22.002 --> 01:08:24.002
The most precious price paid.

172
01:08:25.002 --> 01:08:27.002
And do not think that we can pay that back.

173
01:08:27.002 --> 01:08:28.002
We can never pay that back.

174
01:08:29.002 --> 01:08:31.002
We do not have a mortgage with God.

175
01:08:32.002 --> 01:08:38.002
So that we are redeemed and then try step by step to struggle to pay something back.

176
01:08:38.002 --> 01:08:39.002
No, that is not true at all.

177
01:08:40.002 --> 01:08:43.002
God has given this to us.

178
01:08:44.002 --> 01:08:45.002
And why does He do that then?

179
01:08:46.002 --> 01:08:49.002
Why is He so generous as a good, good Father?

180
01:08:50.002 --> 01:08:52.002
Well, the Bible is very clear about this, thankfully.

181
01:08:53.002 --> 01:08:54.002
Because He loves you.

182
01:08:57.002 --> 01:08:58.002
That changes everything.

183
01:08:59.002 --> 01:09:04.002
When you read Matthew 5, He says all of that because He loves you.

184
01:09:05.002 --> 01:09:10.002
And Jesus also says, yes, those things are not for nothing.

185
01:09:12.002 --> 01:09:15.002
Please never give back, do not give back out of a sense of duty.

186
01:09:16.002 --> 01:09:20.002
Or at least let it grow into a response to His love.

187
01:09:21.002 --> 01:09:23.002
For that is true worship.

188
01:09:24.002 --> 01:09:27.002
When we give back and respond to the love of the Father, that is worship.

189
01:09:28.002 --> 01:09:30.002
And then, what happens then?

190
01:09:31.002 --> 01:09:32.002
Then we start to resemble our Father together.

191
01:09:32.002 --> 01:09:33.002
For then we also become generous.

192
01:09:34.002 --> 01:09:37.002
Then we are changed in our way of thinking.

193
01:09:38.002 --> 01:09:43.002
And Jesus says in this text, yes, do not hold back, just go for it.

194
01:09:44.002 --> 01:09:45.002
Give, give, give.

195
01:09:46.002 --> 01:09:47.002
And then He comes again with that promise.

196
01:09:48.002 --> 01:09:53.002
Yes, then He also says, yes, for if you give, I will give back to you abundantly.

197
01:09:54.002 --> 01:09:55.002
Yes, that is true, He says that too, those are His promises.

198
01:09:56.002 --> 01:09:58.002
But that is a love relationship.

199
01:09:59.002 --> 01:10:00.002
Do you understand?

200
01:10:01.002 --> 01:10:05.002
That has nothing to do with the things they say here in this world.

201
01:10:06.002 --> 01:10:07.002
That has nothing to do with it at all.

202
01:10:08.002 --> 01:10:13.002
What matters is that we can obtain that full life from Jesus.

203
01:10:14.002 --> 01:10:17.002
But also that from that full life, we can sow from that abundance.

204
01:10:18.002 --> 01:10:22.002
For I want to emphasize that you cannot give what you do not have.

205
01:10:23.002 --> 01:10:26.002
So let God give you seed to sow.

206
01:10:26.002 --> 01:10:29.002
And give God the space for that in your life, that is something we may do.

207
01:10:30.002 --> 01:10:31.002
And then go and do that.

208
01:10:32.002 --> 01:10:37.002
Start small and then go all out, just as Jesus invites us to.

209
01:10:38.002 --> 01:10:43.002
And I would like to dedicate this collection to our good, good Father.

210
01:10:44.002 --> 01:10:46.002
And perhaps it is nice to stand for that.

211
01:10:47.002 --> 01:10:48.002
That we stand for our Father.

212
01:10:50.002 --> 01:10:51.002
Thank you, Lord.

213
01:10:52.002 --> 01:10:53.002
You are God.

214
01:10:53.002 --> 01:10:57.002
Lord, we do not preach a false abundance gospel.

215
01:10:58.002 --> 01:11:00.002
But we preach the pure abundance gospel.

216
01:11:01.002 --> 01:11:02.002
Because you already have everything.

217
01:11:03.002 --> 01:11:04.002
Everything already belongs to you.

218
01:11:05.002 --> 01:11:06.002
And you care for your children.

219
01:11:07.002 --> 01:11:08.002
Lord, and I thank you for that.

220
01:11:09.002 --> 01:11:11.002
And I also thank you, Lord, as we act and walk in faith.

221
01:11:12.002 --> 01:11:14.002
As we are also called.

222
01:11:15.002 --> 01:11:17.002
Lord, then you will fulfill your promises.

223
01:11:18.002 --> 01:11:21.002
And those promises of the eternal, the promises of the good, good Father are true.

224
01:11:21.002 --> 01:11:22.002
They are pure.

225
01:11:23.002 --> 01:11:25.002
Like silver that has been refined in a furnace.

226
01:11:26.002 --> 01:11:27.002
Seven times purified.

227
01:11:28.002 --> 01:11:31.002
So the promises of God will be without impurities.

228
01:11:32.002 --> 01:11:36.002
And also that which God sows in you is pure, is clean, is clear.

229
01:11:37.002 --> 01:11:39.002
And I bless us with this as an open church.

230
01:11:40.002 --> 01:11:42.002
That we may sow pure and clean.

231
01:11:43.002 --> 01:11:46.002
And also may become pure and clean through what Jesus has done for us.

232
01:11:47.002 --> 01:11:48.002
In the name of Jesus.

233
01:11:49.002 --> 01:11:50.002
Much blessing in giving.

234
01:11:51.002 --> 01:11:52.002
Thank you very much.

235
01:12:21.002 --> 01:12:26.002
I had so much great information that it would not be right to rush through it.

236
01:12:27.002 --> 01:12:28.002
To do it too quickly.

237
01:12:29.002 --> 01:12:35.002
So I asked Bram, can you give a piece of teaching this Sunday about Ezra 1 to 6.

238
01:12:36.002 --> 01:12:38.002
But just anything, anything from Ezra.

239
01:12:39.002 --> 01:12:43.002
And it also touched me greatly that, I don't know if you can still remember this.

240
01:12:44.002 --> 01:12:47.002
But last Sunday, last Sunday we took communion together.

241
01:12:47.002 --> 01:12:52.002
And Robert did the communion based on the Passover lamb from Ezra.

242
01:12:53.002 --> 01:12:55.002
And then I thought, yes, this is so cool.

243
01:12:56.002 --> 01:12:59.002
Because, then Robert said, because Tim will surely talk about that.

244
01:13:00.002 --> 01:13:01.002
And I was like, yes.

245
01:13:02.002 --> 01:13:07.002
But that is because when you rush something, when you do something in a hurry.

246
01:13:08.002 --> 01:13:09.002
Then you might catch the big lines.

247
01:13:10.002 --> 01:13:12.002
But God's Word is so deep, it is so rich.

248
01:13:13.002 --> 01:13:15.002
Then we can draw so many deep, beautiful words out.

249
01:13:15.002 --> 01:13:17.002
So I am hungry for what Bram is going to bring.

250
01:13:18.002 --> 01:13:22.002
And I would like it if we really take this to heart.

251
01:13:23.002 --> 01:13:25.002
Because the Word of God must change us.

